00:44:44,720 --> 00:44:47,180
There we go.

877
00:44:47,180 --> 00:44:51,320
So I've given you an
introduction to GT Sophy,

878
00:44:51,320 --> 00:44:54,060
but I'm going to tell you a
little bit more about it now

879
00:44:54,060 --> 00:44:56,000
and then I'll pause
for questions.

880
00:44:56,000 --> 00:44:58,620
So again, to remind
you, this is the work

881
00:44:58,620 --> 00:45:02,380
that was done at Sony AI on
racing champion Gran Turismo

882
00:45:02,380 --> 00:45:04,467
drivers with deep
reinforcement learning.

883
00:45:04,467 --> 00:45:06,050
So this is going to
that other extreme

884
00:45:06,050 --> 00:45:08,610
where we now do
have a simulation.

885
00:45:08,610 --> 00:45:11,950
And actually the whole task is
to do well in the simulation.

886
00:45:11,950 --> 00:45:13,610
So this is not
embodiment anymore.

887
00:45:13,610 --> 00:45:19,650
This is to build a real
world-class world-expert agent

888
00:45:19,650 --> 00:45:23,050
at race car driving.

889
00:45:23,050 --> 00:45:25,190
And I showed you
this slide already.

890
00:45:25,190 --> 00:45:29,930
But the success was just like
in the success cases of chess

891
00:45:29,930 --> 00:45:34,292
and poker and Go, it relied on
